--- Rosetta Code: Quine
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Quine
--- The text of the program is held in s, with an at sign where s itself is
--- written; it is printed with that sign replaced by s between quotes, the
--- sign and the quote made from their character codes.
use bits
q = char[39]
s = '--- Rosetta Code: Quine
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Quine
--- The text of the program is held in s, with an at sign where s itself is
--- written; it is printed with that sign replaced by s between quotes, the
--- sign and the quote made from their character codes.
use bits
q = char[39]
s = @
log[replace[s, char[64], concat[[q, s, q]]]]'
log[replace[s, char[64], concat[[q, s, q]]]]
